## Orientation (C30)

**Portrait only, one-handed.** Phone upright, single-thumb play. Android portrait lock (no autorotate); Windows uses the same portrait-aspect layout in a tall window. Board on top, every primary action (Lock In, Time Card, path taps) in the bottom thumb zone. All older "landscape" notes are void.

## High-speed rail / 高铁 (C31)

Side-of-map rail. Board + ride; Shoot while riding; car bulletproof; **1× per match**. Confirmed design, **deferred from 14-day ship (C34)**. Numerics still OPEN in PRODUCT_MEMORY.

## Snap Shot targeting (C32)

Snap resolves at its **completion** second and wounds only a pawn on the **aimed tile** with clear LoS — it does not sweep the line. Lanes are Hold Angle's job (Day 6). LoS = integer Bresenham on tiles, same floor, endpoints excluded; **never** a physics raycast.

## Match pool / Time Card (C33)

One **shared** match Time Resource pool (demo **900s**). Each round one side plays a **Time Card** committing **N** seconds; round 1 = Attacker, then **alternates**. Both sides Program simultaneously inside **N**. **N spent in full** (unused burned). Positions + wounds **carry** across rounds. Match ends on Dead or when pool cannot fund another MinRound. Time Card ≠ gear card.

